<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Azzi-Hayasa</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 BCE – 1290 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Azzi-Hayasa, a mountain confederation of north-eastern Anatolia that fought the Hittites in the 14th century BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Hayasa and Azzi were lands in the highlands of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzurum">Erzurum</a> region. They appear in Hittite records from the 15th century BCE as a federation of mountain communities beyond the Hittite frontier.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of its internal structure. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suppiluliuma-i">Suppiluliuma I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> made a treaty with Hukkana of Hayasa and gave him his sister in marriage, with strict rules about Hittite customs. Some scholars connect Hayasa with the Armenian name for <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/armenia">Armenia</a>, Hay, though this is disputed.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mursili-ii">Mursili II</a> fought Anniya of Azzi in long campaigns, and Hayasa disappears from the record in the 13th century BCE. The highlands later formed part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nairi">Nairi</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-urartu">Kingdom of Urartu</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/azzi-hayasa.jpg" alt="Azzi-Hayasa" width="320" height="400"><figcaption>Image: Mx. Granger · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hittite_Cuneiform_Tablet-_Legal_Deposition(%3F).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 BCE – 1290 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century-bce">16th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hukkana, Anniya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>, <a href="/countries/armenia">Armenia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hayasa-Azzi, Hayasa, Azzi-Hayasa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1395&amp;focus=azzi-hayasa" aria-label="Azzi-Hayasa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5643 759 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Azzi-Hayasa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5963 1015L5852 1002"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5852 1002h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5963 1015h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5963 1015h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=-1395&amp;focus=azzi-hayasa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

